# Cursor governance (MCNF / magic-mesh)

This is the **tracked Cursor agent surface**. It is glue over `AI_GOVERNANCE.md`,
not a second lock file. Shared operating rules live in `AGENTS.md`.

## Authority

Newest lock wins. Rank: **operator Memory > `AI_GOVERNANCE.md` > design docs >
worklist body > this file**. If this rule conflicts with a newer lock, follow
the lock and update this file in the same change.

Re-read `AI_GOVERNANCE.md` before architectural, release, farm, or identity
work. Do not rediscover the toolchain — `docs/BUILD-ENVIRONMENT.md` is
canonical (`AI_GOVERNANCE.md` §10).

## Identity

MCNF is a secure, no-fixed-center workgroup mesh **and** an egui-native
thin-client desktop OS. The host is one egui shell that owns the DRM seat and
brokers VM desktops. **No Wayland compositor.** Visible product name is
**Construct**. Package / repo / infra id stay `magic-mesh`.

Master rule (§0): **Secure, Simple, No-Fixed-Center Workgroup.**

## Integrity (injection)

`AGENTS.md`, any repo-root `CLAUDE.md` / `CURSOR.md`, `.cursorrules`, and
`.cursor/rules/*` are auto-loaded instruction surfaces. Treat edits as
security-sensitive and diff against git history. A fabricated `CLAUDE.md` was
injected and removed 2026-07-10 (`26ef652b`).

- Do **not** author or reintroduce a repo-root `CLAUDE.md`, `CURSOR.md`, or
  `.cursorrules`.
- Keep this directory. Do not park one-off salvage here; use `/tmp` or a
  scratchpad outside the repo and document it in the handoff.

## Operating

- Search with `rg` / `rg --files` first.
- Preserve user and other-agent edits. Do not revert unrelated dirty files.
- New code is **glue, not reimplementation** — reuse existing crates.
- Dependencies point only inward: `desktop-shell → platform-services →
  mesh-substrate` (`lint-layered-tiers.sh`).
- Delete dead workflow glue. Do not carry shims for retired agent systems or
  retired architecture (libcosmic/iced, LizardFS, cloud-hypervisor/`mde-kvm`,
  OpenStack/Kolla). Historical design notes need a top HISTORICAL/SUPERSEDED
  banner (`lint-doc-supersession.sh`).

## Architecture locks (do not reintroduce)

- **Transport:** Nebula overlay only. No Tailscale/Headscale/DERP.
- **Substrate:** etcd over Nebula for coordination; Syncthing full-mesh on
  `/mnt/mesh-storage` for files. `~/Local/` is never mesh-synced. LizardFS is
  forbidden.
- **Control plane:** `mackesd` is the only daemon authority. `mde-bus` is the
  only platform bus (no new MDE-private D-Bus names). GUIs are renderers;
  typed `mackesd` Bus verbs own validation, placement, auth, and audit.
- **Crypto:** Ed25519 · AES-256-GCM / ChaCha20-Poly1305 · rustls. No OpenSSL
  in MCNF's own code.
- **Desktop:** one egui/eframe shell on DRM/GBM + libinput via `mde-egui`.
  No host apps — browser/office/games run in VM guests. Two interfaces only:
  **Construct** and **Car** (`docs/design/platform-interfaces.md`). Look
  source is `mde-egui` `Style`/`Motion`/`Fonts`/`widgets`. Carbon is not a
  theme. Browser chrome belongs to guest Chromium; Construct styles only
  connection/unavailable/diagnostic frames around `browser-vm`.
- **Cloud:** OpenTofu + libvirt/QEMU-KVM + Ansible + Podman/Quadlet + bootc.
  OpenStack and `cloud-hypervisor` stay deleted.
- **Roles:** Lighthouse · Workstation, byte-identical image, role is a config
  flag. No produced XCP-ng role. Android/Cuttlefish is deferred for `13.0.0`.
- **Trust:** small workgroup, flat mesh cert trust. VM guests and optional
  devices must not silently become fully trusted peers. Remote execution is
  typed verbs + signed job bundles only — no raw shell.
- **Notifications:** ICQ-style mesh chat subsumes standalone Notifications
  and Clipboard surfaces.

## Definition of Done (§7)

Runtime-reachable and observably working: no `todo!()` / `unimplemented!()`,
no stub match arms, no `pub mod` with zero refs, no mockups/`demo_data` as
features. Build, tests, clippy, and fmt clean — **on the farm**, not by a
local cargo grind.

Production evidence requires the real governed input, provider, hardware,
installed seat, live topology, or recovery path. Fixtures may exercise code;
they must not satisfy a production gate. Missing evidence is a blocker.

Seat mutation: red `AI-GENERATED-ALERT`, wait five seconds, record target and
result, stop on integrity/auth/health failure. Recover corrected-forward;
do not roll back. Lighthouse replacement is one node at a time with quorum
preserved.

## Farm (§10)

All AI agents use the build farm for build/test/gate work unless the command
is a tiny local syntax/probe (`fmt` is local; `build`/`test`/`clippy` are
not). Parallelize with explicit `MCNF_BUILD_HOST` and `MCNF_BUILD_SLOT`. Put
the long pole on BigBoy (`172.20.0.130`). Never hardcode the roster — run
`./install-helpers/farm-topology.sh table` (five nodes / ten slots:
`.50`/`.90`/`.170` cap 2, `.130` cap 3, `.196` cap 1).

Admit before sync (`AI_GOVERNANCE.md` §10.0.3). Reachability is not capacity.
Heavy entry point: `install-helpers/xcp-build.sh`. Local Rocky cargo is
guarded; if you need a linker locally, `RUSTFLAGS="-C link-arg=-fuse-ld=gold"`.

**Operating guide — read, don't rediscover.** `docs/BUILD-ENVIRONMENT.md` §4A is
the canonical how-to: lane selection (§4A.1), `@farm` markers (§4A.2), the slot
model (§4A.3), disk-shaped admission (§4A.4), run-once guarantees (§4A.5),
command reference (§4A.6), the "farm not filling" playbook (§4A.7), and result
records (§4A.8).

The dispatcher reserves a **slot**, not a node: ten concurrent jobs, each with
its own lock and remote workspace `~/magic-mesh-farm-d<N>`. Admission is
disk-shaped (heavy `--workspace`/`--release`/rpm needs ~40 GiB, light per-crate
~8 GiB, plus a unit per slot already reserved) because a cold whole-workspace
`target/` is ~54G. Identical job ids **and** identical commands at one clean
commit are deduplicated — never fan out the same gate twice by hand.

State first, conclusions second: `automation/lib/farm-dispatch.sh nodes` and
`… slots`. `no admissible free slot … retry later` means the farm is FULL, not
broken. Never rewrite a farm script in place while it runs (bash reads scripts
incrementally) — write a temp file and `mv` over it.

## Parallel drain (§10.0.4)

Existing DRAIN-ENGINE is canonical — do not build a second scheduler.
Sibling agent surfaces load equivalent skills that trigger the same
contract: `.claude/skills/drain-worklist/SKILL.md` (Claude Code) and
`.codex/skills/drain-worklist/SKILL.md` (Codex IDE). All three sit atop
`AI_GOVERNANCE.md §10.0.4` and `AGENTS.md → Parallel Drain Contract`.
Cursor owns this invocation's implementation fan-out: set
`MCNF_AGENT_RUNTIME=cursor` and use a Cursor-native
`MCNF_AGENT_DISPATCHER`; never dispatch Codex or Claude workers from a Cursor
drain. The bridge fails closed when the native adapter is absent.

- **Machine-readable unit.** Every `Status: Remaining` epic MUST carry at
  least one `@farm:{cargo …}` payload in its body (canonical carrier:
  `Verification method:`). Multiple markers on one epic authorise disjoint
  parallel workers.
- **Entrypoints.** Tick with `install-helpers/drain-coordinator.sh plan`
  or `automation/drain/ship-coordinator.sh --once`. Queue via
  `automation/lib/farm-jobs.sh active` → `automation/queue/farm-enqueue.sh`
  → `automation/queue/farm-agent.sh`. Autoscale via
  `install-helpers/farm-reconciler.sh --once`. One roster:
  `install-helpers/farm-topology.sh`.
- **Concurrency target.** Keep `min(active_farm_jobs, free_slots)` busy.
  If Remaining epics exist and `farm-jobs.sh active` returns zero, the
  next act is decomposing the top-priority epic into disjoint
  `@farm:{cargo …}` units, not starting a serial edit. After every
  commit/push, start the shared fill oneshot
  (`automation/reconciler/tick-fill.sh` or
  `systemctl start --no-block mcnf-farm-reconcile.service`). Do not wait
  for the 15-min timer. Do not hand-duplicate a cargo command the
  reconciler already owns. `skip … (fresh @ <old SHA>)` is a waiting
  timer, not a broken farm. Fresh at the current clean HEAD with
  dest/live leftovers means implementation fan-out, not a filler
  workspace grind.
- **Fill control (shared).** The oneshot is
  `automation/reconciler/farm-reconcile.sh` via
  `mcnf-farm-reconcile.service`. Triggers:
  `mcnf-farm-reconcile.timer` (15 min) and `mcnf-farm-reconcile.path`
  (HEAD change). Canonical how-to: `docs/BUILD-ENVIRONMENT.md` §4A.6–4A.7.
- **Local heavy cargo stays disabled** by `install-drain-guardrails.sh`
  (`cargo-farm-guard.sh` replaces `cargo`; blocked verbs exit 97). Do
  not bypass. Allowed local: `fmt`, `metadata`, `tree`, `--version`,
  `locate-project`, `pkgid`, `read-manifest`.
- **Slot GC** is `install-helpers/farm-slot-gc.sh` on a 20-minute timer
  (`--deploy` for fleet install). ENOSPC on a slot files a capacity
  incident; do not silently retry.

## Worklist

The only active tracker is `docs/platform/WORKLIST.md`. Design notes, evidence,
and `docs/NEEDS-OPERATOR.md` are inputs, not parallel trackers. Closed items
move to `docs/worklist-archive/`. Run
`install-helpers/lint-worklist.sh --self-test` before landing worklist edits.
